WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:02.190
Let's talk about Donald Trump's tax returns.

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.190
Briefly.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:07.910
The situation with Donald Trump's tax returns
is escalating to the point where Donald Trump

00:00:07.910 --> 00:00:14.330
is now effectively begging the Supreme court
to hide his tax returns from investigators.

00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:19.850
And this is hilarious, but it's also very
important in terms of what is quickly becoming

00:00:19.850 --> 00:00:24.430
a battle, really about the separation of powers
in the United States and about checks and

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:25.430
balances.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.960
So I'll catch you up and then we'll get to
the news.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:32.170
Investigators have a criminal probe going
into Donald Trump and his businesses finances.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:37.590
They've tried to obtain Donald Trump's tax
returns and his business tax returns for this

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:38.590
investigation.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:39.980
Trump tried to block it.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:42.870
Multiple courts have already okayed it.

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:45.640
The next step is the Supreme court.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.850
And indeed Donald Trump has filed for an appeal
to the Supreme court.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:54.980
Now, what's important with the Supreme court
is they're not required to take the case at

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:55.980
all.

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:58.510
They're not required to review the ruling
of the lower court.

00:00:58.510 --> 00:01:00.440
In this case, it's the second district court.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.160
The Supreme court might decide we're not going
to take the case.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:09.110
Um, and in that situation, the lower court
ruling would stand, which in this particular

00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:15.820
situation is a ruling that says Trump has
to provide the tax returns to the investigators.

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:22.740
Importantly, the Supreme court currently has
to Trump selections, Neil Neil Gorsuch and

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.490
the absolute lunatic Brett Kavanaugh.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:29.240
The Supreme court is going to announce in
the next few weeks if they will review the

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.530
case if they agree to review the case.

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:34.630
That review probably will happen before the
2020 election.

00:01:34.630 --> 00:01:36.250
Now there is breaking news on this.

00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:42.080
The Supreme court did yesterday impose an
indefinite delay, uh, on the house of representatives

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:47.409
demand for president Trump's financial records
to give them time to figure out how to handle

00:01:47.409 --> 00:01:51.610
the dispute until they decide what is going
to happen with this case, that case.

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:57.740
The other case related to Donald Trump's taxes,
but this is a major separation of powers case

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:02.241
because if the Supreme court does take the
case and they decide, you know what, Trump

00:02:02.241 --> 00:02:08.610
does not have to turn over his tax returns,
what does that say about our checks and balances?

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:10.979
The checks and balances in our system?

00:02:10.979 --> 00:02:19.510
What does it say about Donald Trump's ability
to or not to have to obey prevailing laws?

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:24.010
It also relates to this issue of Donald Trump's
immunity.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:29.720
Trump's lawyers claim that Donald Trump has
immunity, not just from prosecution, but even

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:31.650
from investigation.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.630
That is a very loose reading of any law that
you can find.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:39.290
And a big piece of all of this is going to
come down to that because remember, we were

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:44.090
told, and even Robert Mueller said at the
conclusion during his testimony and and in

00:02:44.090 --> 00:02:50.320
the Mueller report, that he did not take a
position on whether Donald Trump should be

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.460
indicted on obstruction of justice because
it is the policy via memo.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:59.380
It has not been legally tested, but it is
the policy via memo of the justice department

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.630
not to prosecute a sitting president.

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:02.630
That's layer one.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:03.630
We could, we could argue that.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:08.290
We could debate that there is this further
position that Donald Trump's lawyers are trying

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:13.970
to argue that Donald Trump's taxes and his
business taxes should not be provided to investigators

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.080
in New York.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:16.080
Why?

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:19.810
Because Donald Trump is immune even from investigation.

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:24.030
And I have read no seriously legal opinion
that agrees with that.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:28.720
And then of course we go back to the bigger
picture on the merits.

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:35.351
Anybody working this hard to hide their tax
returns has something to hide that is very,

00:03:35.351 --> 00:03:36.400
very serious.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:37.950
We don't have to go through that.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:45.819
Once again, I don't believe that Donald Trump's
taxes would expose criminality, although arguably

00:03:45.819 --> 00:03:50.870
a double accounting and one set of books for
loan purposes and one set of books for tax

00:03:50.870 --> 00:03:54.890
purposes in New York state is actually against
the law.

00:03:54.890 --> 00:03:59.200
I believe the most likely scenario is that
Donald Trump would be exposed as not being

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:01.370
as wealthy as he claims to be.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:05.620
I believe that Donald Trump's shady business
dealings, which are the subject of much speculation

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:10.260
with all sorts of different countries, could
be Russia, Saudi Arabia and others would potentially

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.940
be exposed.

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:16.359
And uh, it would be both, uh, personally embarrassing
to Trump and also problematic for him.

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:21.180
I don't know that it's a shoe in that there
is actual criminality or at least definitive

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:24.849
criminality that would be exposed by Trump's
tax returns.

00:04:24.849 --> 00:04:26.310
Although I certainly wouldn't rule it out.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:29.740
And it wouldn't come as a surprise given everything
that has gone on.

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:30.740
So my questions to you.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:36.779
Number one, why do you believe that Donald
Trump has been working so hard for so long

00:04:36.779 --> 00:04:38.949
to prevent the release of his tax returns?

00:04:38.949 --> 00:04:44.800
Number two, what do you believe will ultimately
happen with this case and the release of Trump's

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:45.800
taxes?

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:46.870
Will the Supreme court take the case?

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:47.870
Let me know what you think.

